Fix these two issues:

## 1. Fix decimal values — max 2 decimal places
Everywhere in the app where macro values are displayed 
(protein, carbs, fat, calories), round to max 2 decimals.

Apply this fix globally in all pages and components:

// Helper function — add to utils/calculateMacros.js
export const round2 = (val) => {
  if (val === null || val === undefined) return 0
  return Math.round(Number(val) * 100) / 100
}

Then wherever macros are displayed, wrap in round2():
- In Home.jsx macro cards
- In Diary.jsx meal entries  
- In Progress.jsx table and charts
- In Scan.jsx result cards
- In Weekly Report macro summary table

Specifically fix the carbs value showing as:
"441.79999999999995" → should show "441.80"

Also fix the macro summary cards showing "LOW" 
incorrectly — recalculate based on actual vs goal.

## 2. Fix PDF duplicate content on page break
The PDF is showing content twice when it spans 2 pages.
This is caused by the addImage being called incorrectly 
for page 2.

Replace the entire PDF generation with this clean approach
that scales the whole report to fit in exactly 1 page:

const downloadPDF = async () => {
  setDownloading(true)

  // Hide download button during capture
  const btn = document.getElementById('pdf-download-btn')
  if (btn) btn.style.display = 'none'

  const reportEl = document.getElementById('weekly-report')

  const canvas = await html2canvas(reportEl, {
    scale: 2,
    backgroundColor: '#fdf6f2',
    useCORS: true,
    logging: false
  })

  // Always fit entire report into 1 A4 page
  const pdf = new jsPDF({
    orientation: 'portrait',
    unit: 'px',
    format: 'a4'
  })

  const pageWidth = pdf.internal.pageSize.getWidth()
  const pageHeight = pdf.internal.pageSize.getHeight()

  // Scale image to fit page width, then check height
  const imgWidth = pageWidth
  const imgHeight = (canvas.height * pageWidth) / canvas.width

  if (imgHeight <= pageHeight) {
    // Fits in 1 page perfectly
    pdf.addImage(
      canvas.toDataURL('image/png'),
      'PNG', 0, 0, imgWidth, imgHeight
    )
  } else {
    // Scale down to fit in 1 page
    const scale = pageHeight / imgHeight
    const scaledWidth = imgWidth * scale
    const scaledHeight = pageHeight
    const xOffset = (pageWidth - scaledWidth) / 2
    pdf.addImage(
      canvas.toDataURL('image/png'),
      'PNG', xOffset, 0, scaledWidth, scaledHeight
    )
  }

  pdf.save(`CalSnap-Weekly-Report-${
    new Date().toISOString().slice(0, 10)
  }.pdf`)

  // Restore download button
  if (btn) btn.style.display = ''
  setDownloading(false)
}

Make sure the download button has id="pdf-download-btn"

